{%- comment -%}
  =========================================================================
  SECTION 4: GHOST_TRANSLATION test plan

  This finding type queries the Translations API, not theme files.
  You need actual translation data in the store with no translation
  app installed.

  Option A — Manual via Shopify Admin:
    1. Go to Settings > Languages in your dev store
    2. Add a secondary language (e.g., French)
    3. Go to a product and add French translations for title/description
    4. Leave the translations in place
    5. Make sure NO translation app is installed
    6. Run a Ghost Code scan — should detect GHOST_TRANSLATION findings

  Option B — Via GraphQL (Admin API):
    1. Enable a locale: mutation { shopLocaleEnable(locale: "fr") { ... } }
    2. Register translations via translationsRegister mutation
    3. Ensure no translation app is installed
    4. Run scan

  Note: Ghost Code needs read_translations scope granted by the merchant.
  In your dev store, re-install the app or trigger the scope request flow.
  =========================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}


